  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 207 PM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nThe long term period is shaping up to be unseasonably warm for the \ncounty warning area (CWA). A persistent weak upper-level ridge is \nforecast to be over the region Friday through early next week. High \ntemperatures are forecast in the 90s on Friday and climb to triple \ndigits Saturday through the remainder of the forecast period. Late \nFriday into Saturday will be our best chance for precipitation due \nto weak shortwave passages. Probability of Precipitation (PoPs) is \nonly around 15% for the northwest CWA, so little relief from the hot \ntemperatures is expected. \n\nFire weather potential will be something to monitor for throughout \nthe week. Currently, fuels are dry throughout the entire CWA. \nRelative humidity (RH) values are forecast in the low 20s for the \nwestern CWA Saturday and slowly creep down to the mid to high teens \nthrough Monday. Afternoon wind gusts up to 30 mph are possible for \nthe western CWA, but lowest RH values and strongest wind gusts are \nnot forecast to coincide, but a few hours of critical fire \nweather conditions could still be possible given the dry fuels \nand unseasonably warm temperatures. \n\nLooking further ahead, models are beginning to show a strong ridge \nset up over the Tri-State area Monday and remain overhead throughout \nnext week. This would support another round of unseasonably warm \ntemperatures and dry conditions for the region.",
